From 9fb8db759832b5056dfbf646543dd766827c8147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Mellmann <flix@benfm.de>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 14:41:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: rockchip: add minimal RV1106 support

Add initial platform support for the Rockchip RV1106 SoC (single
Cortex-A7, GIC-400). This is a minimal bringup without clock or
pinctrl drivers - relies on U-Boot leaving peripherals configured.

What works:
- Boot to interactive shell on UART2 (ttyS2, 115200 baud)
- Native 8250_dw serial driver with interrupts
- ARMv7 generic timer at 24 MHz
- GIC-400 interrupt controller
- VFP/NEON for hard-float userland
- Initramfs (xz compressed) boot

New files:
- rv1106.dtsi: minimal SoC device tree (CPU, GIC, timer, UART2)
- rv1106-evb.dts: board DTS (256 MiB RAM, UART2 console)
- rv1106.c: minimal machine descriptor
- rv1106_defconfig: lightweight kernel config
- rv1106-fitimage.its: FIT image source for mkimage

Introduces temporary ARCH_ROCKCHIP_RV1106 Kconfig to avoid pulling
in the full Rockchip platform dependencies (PINCTRL, L2X0, REGULATOR,
SMP) that are not yet needed or applicable.

Tested on Luckfox Pico Max (RV1106G3) with Yocto 6.0 initramfs.

Signed-off-by: Felix Mellmann <flix@benfm.de>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [still under development]
